## Phoenix preserves failed-task status in experiment traces

Source: Arize AI · Phoenix GitHub release — https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/releases/tag/%40arizeai/phoenix-client%407.18.1
Published: 2026-11-04
Channel: github

Phoenix is an AI observability and evaluation platform whose client records experiment tasks as trace spans, records of individual operations. A client patch fixes those records so failed tasks retain their error status. The same patch preserves system and developer instructions when converting prompts to Anthropic, while omitting empty text blocks from the system array. These are narrow correctness fixes: the release note does not describe a broader evaluation redesign or quantify the impact on earlier experiments.

Why it matters: For Phoenix experiment users: verify a deliberately failing task remains marked as failed, and inspect converted instructions when comparing model behavior.

