## OpenInference keeps output and token counts when model streams fail

Source: Arize AI · OpenInference GitHub release — https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference/releases/tag/%40arizeai/openinference-instrumentation-openai%404.4.3
Published: 2026-11-04
Channel: github

OpenInference provides instrumentation that records AI model activity in traces. Its JavaScript OpenAI integration now retains output and token counts from Responses streams that end incomplete or failed. A span is the trace record for one operation; previously, these streams left an error-marked span without the output or usage that could explain what happened.

The change expands which final stream events the integration keeps. It previously retained only the completed event. It now also records the response carried by incomplete and failed events, so their output and token information remain available. The release gives reaching the output-token limit as an example of an incomplete response.

Status handling still distinguishes the two cases. A failed response remains an error, while an incomplete response is recorded like a completed one. Consequently, the presence of recorded output does not mean a model finished its requested work. The release documents a telemetry correction, without claiming that it prevents model failures or changes the provider’s response.

Why it matters: For teams reviewing streaming costs or failures: test incomplete and failed responses separately, and check response state alongside span status.

